abstract: >
  Materials for a hands-on workshop introducing researchers
  to the Unix/Linux command line. The workshop develops
  foundational skills for working with research computing
  environments, including high-performance computing (HPC)
  systems, cloud platforms, and data-intensive workflows.

  Participants learn how to navigate file systems, create
  and manage files and directories, work efficiently with
  the shell, use command-line tools to inspect and process
  data, and automate repetitive tasks through shell
  scripting.

  No prior command-line experience is assumed. By the end of
  the workshop, participants will be able to use the command
  line confidently for common research computing tasks and
  will understand how command-line skills support
  reproducible, scalable, and efficient research workflows.
